{"event_type":"review","id":"31dac31a8979355fe961bb79f3d0e4b0d6caa27003147c8b4dcc7eceef92256f","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T03:17:37Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c0ca6b55ff17d64c16154c63498c9f7e3614546b25f54bfc2994333989a977c2","sha256":"c0ca6b55ff17d64c16154c63498c9f7e3614546b25f54bfc2994333989a977c2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f94c534a2bcddd1812bb42179637e9a86c5fa54ed77cdbfd53605f776b30eafa","sha256":"f94c534a2bcddd1812bb42179637e9a86c5fa54ed77cdbfd53605f776b30eafa"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c920171b42f66dd26e2a1783dd4a89ef6dca609cf49a309b6f4ef3ae24510646","sha256":"c920171b42f66dd26e2a1783dd4a89ef6dca609cf49a309b6f4ef3ae24510646"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7625488a4645edce6c58072ee655ec40a6bdc97caa0fe15122a9cd3f746a8c2f","sha256":"7625488a4645edce6c58072ee655ec40a6bdc97caa0fe15122a9cd3f746a8c2f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f568ea5452f9340c3c806e62a3db860d2db595b776dce67109e4c54a37df2061","sha256":"f568ea5452f9340c3c806e62a3db860d2db595b776dce67109e4c54a37df2061"}],"attempt_id":"f9131c286677310d9e8590f742de90dbe24f81adedf5ac94d29ccf9a412bdd2b:0:1","base":"fb26a59a912047f12b55f6f8e7d23321c7062c50","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"96452966aeb98a691b430c7c028421743e07d1bf","body":"**Enforce `Budget.maxOutputTokens` and `Budget.maxContextTokens`, or stop accepting them.**\n\nThe driver declares both caps as optional budget fields, and its docs say they stop runs. The supplied source shows no code that reads them. A caller that sets either cap therefore gets no stop at that cap. Output and context spend can exceed the declared limit. Only the other stop conditions bound the run.\n\nThe fix needs a design decision, so it is not a localized patch. Add a stop condition for each cap that uses the usage counters the driver README defines. Alternatively, reject these fields in the budget schema until enforcement exists. Either option must state which provider usage fields count toward each cap.","id":"1e3116324fb600ebbe01a5381a88d510f31af53c60a74ed088a305449e2c93e2","intervals":[],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Enforce `Budget.maxOutputTokens` and `Budget.maxContextTokens`, or stop accepting them."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"96452966aeb98a691b430c7c028421743e07d1bf","body":"**Unwrap `RetryError` before the ceiling-refusal check.**\n\nWith `maxRetries: 1` (`src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts:1043`), a retryable first attempt can be followed by a refused retry. The SDK then wraps that second failure in a `RetryError`, so `isPreRequestCeilingRefusal(err)` at `src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts:1364` returns false. The refusal falls through to the generic error path. `classifyRunFailure` finds no `APICallError` or `TimeoutError` in the wrapper and returns `'unknown'`. A budget refusal can therefore settle as `error` instead of `budget`, and a harness refusal loses its diagnostic class.\n\nBefore the check at line 1364, extract the refusal from the `RetryError` by walking `errors` last-first and then `cause`. Follow the existing `apiErrorsIn` walk. The branch body must read the extracted refusal's `kind` and fields, not `err`. The repair catch at `src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts:1844` uses `maxRetries: 0`, so the SDK rethrows without wrapping and needs no change.","id":"3502190fba04eaac5ec4f1e9385306f1184c8524f3884ae14f26742f0cdf5240","intervals":[],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Unwrap `RetryError` before the ceiling-refusal check."}],"head":"65ce54d449bae7f0a1bb12a15e82cfbda05eac55","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"7f1172bf44415e31dcb3d126205cdd929c112056","intervals":[[16,16],[19,19],[49,49],[51,51],[55,62],[109,111],[123,126],[152,155],[171,171],[178,179],[190,190],[193,193],[199,200],[202,204],[260,260],[263,267],[286,286],[291,297],[336,336],[362,363],[366,367],[378,378],[382,384],[387,389],[399,400],[428,429],[447,449],[461,463]],"path":"scripts/dd1-abort-spike.mjs"},{"blob":"96452966aeb98a691b430c7c028421743e07d1bf","intervals":[[11,19],[22,25],[28,48],[56,66],[72,77],[99,123],[142,143],[153,182],[188,208],[215,215],[218,220],[225,226],[228,238],[241,250],[253,267],[269,271],[277,278],[284,286],[290,330],[334,363],[373,380],[389,412],[422,422],[425,425],[428,436],[444,448],[450,463],[465,470],[473,484],[486,535],[540,558],[560,652],[656,660],[686,690],[692,759],[761,806],[808,956],[966,966],[969,981],[988,1013],[1016,1213],[1215,1216],[1226,1229],[1231,1280],[1283,1291],[1293,1304],[1307,1314],[1316,1317],[1325,1336],[1339,1391],[1394,1395],[1400,1402],[1405,1406],[1409,1413],[1420,1950],[1952,1952],[1955,1958],[1962,1962],[1965,1965],[1972,1976],[1990,2057],[2063,2071],[2085,2115],[2117,2118],[2121,2126],[2130,2132],[2134,2134],[2136,2142],[2144,2167],[2180,2182],[2196,2199],[2201,2251],[2254,2254],[2256,2256],[2275,2278],[2308,2331],[2353,2353],[2360,2367],[2370,2370],[2414,2763]],"path":"src/driver/ai-sdk/index.ts"}],"job_id":"f9131c286677310d9e8590f742de90dbe24f81adedf5ac94d29ccf9a412bdd2b:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"ee8ce9a0590a78024c1eb75a5b1239e54a4609b5","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/dd1-abort-spike.mjs"},"merge":"6a842e1e1bf6ffde44dd9d8f561a01d702b4bb34","method":"pre-merge","pre":"5170bdc4c98ac6712fb87c0109c31445488629f1","source_path":"scripts/dd1-abort-spike.mjs"},"blob":"7f1172bf44415e31dcb3d126205cdd929c112056","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/dd1-abort-spike.mjs","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"5cbc2395cbeb06544b390b318219f8a059a98